  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.644,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Operations with Integers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Additive inverse of an integer a is represented as – a. So the additive inverse of 18 is represented as – (18) = – 18, and the additive inverse of – 18 is represented as – (– 18) = 18."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.168,
            0.505,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.2 Multiplication of Integers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.201,
            0.848,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We used the token model to represent addition and subtraction of integers. We now explore how to model multiplication of integers using tokens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.259,
            0.847,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose we put some positive tokens into an empty bag as shown in the figure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.306,
            0.551,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many positives are in the bag now?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.332,
            0.569,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are 8 positives in the bag. We can see this as adding 2 positives to the bag 4 times. Thus, the operation is, 4 × 2 = 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.39,
            0.571,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen this kind of multiplication of positive integers before. Can we use tokens to give meaning to multiplications like 4 × (– 2)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.579,
            0.309,
            0.858,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.579,
                0.309,
                0.858,
                0.41
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.602,
                0.414,
                0.823,
                0.448
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Two green tokens 4 times = 8 4 × 2 = 8"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.467,
            0.304,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us see how."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.491,
            0.549,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For every new operation, we start with an empty bag."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.529,
            0.549,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4 × (–2) can be interpreted as placing 2 negatives into an empty bag 4 times. We use red tokens for negatives, so we place 2 negatives into an empty bag 4 times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.624,
            0.548,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are now 8 red tokens or 8 negatives in the bag, meaning – 8. 4 × (– 2) = (– 8)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.561,
            0.486,
            0.841,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.561,
                0.486,
                0.841,
                0.586
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.6,
                0.592,
                0.814,
                0.625
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Two red tokens 4 times = – 8 4 × (– 2) = – 8"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.615,
            0.932,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.556,
                0.615,
                0.932,
                0.681
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.696,
            0.846,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Similarly find the values of 4 × (– 6) and 9 × (– 7)? How can we interpret (– 4) × 2?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.741,
            0.846,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the multiplier is positive, we place tokens into the bag. When the multiplier is negative, we "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "remove",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " tokens from the bag."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.78,
            0.847,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, for (– 4) × 2, we need to remove two positives or two green tokens from the bag 4 times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.934,
            0.838,
            0.949
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "29"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
